libjpeg-turbo 3.1.4 -- the JPEG codec of Skia and WebKit, ported to Onyx
=====================================================================

Source: the release tag 3.1.4 of https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo (commit
e352b02f794f701407b39af08576035ba3360d60; the release tarball on the GitHub release page was not
reachable from the build machine -- the tag's tree is the same sources). Licences (LICENSE.md): the IJG
licence, the Modified (3-clause) BSD licence, the zlib licence -- all permissive.

Why it and not the in-tree jpeg-9f (the apps' IJG libjpeg): Skia's JPEG codec and WebKit's JPEG decoder
use libjpeg-turbo's extensions (jpeg_skip_scanlines, jpeg_crop_scanline, the JCS_EXT_* colour spaces);
WebKit's PlayStation / Windows options ask for "JPEG 1.5.2" (a libjpeg-turbo version).

Kept: the library's sources (src/), the AArch64 SIMD (simd/arm, simd/jsimd.h, simd/CMakeLists.txt,
simd/simdcoverage.c -- its CMake names it), the CMake build (CMakeLists.txt, cmakescripts/, release/'s
.in templates), LICENSE.md, README.ijg, README.md, ChangeLog.md. Not kept: the other SIMD back ends
(x86, MIPS, PowerPC), Java, the fuzzers, the test images, doc/, win/, sharedlib/. No change to the
sources.

Built by tools/ports/libjpeg-turbo/build.sh with its CMake and tools/onyx-toolchain.cmake: libjpeg.a
(the libjpeg 6b API, arithmetic coding on, the Neon intrinsics) + jpeglib.h, jconfig.h, jmorecfg.h,
jerror.h + libjpeg.pc into the POSIX sysroot. No TurboJPEG API, no tools, no tests.
